<% content_for :title, 'Rulebook Page Mapping' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Rulebook Page Mapping' do %>
  <div class='space-y-8'>

    <p class='text-fg-muted'>
      Every rulebook has a page offset that maps PDF page indices to printed page numbers by
      simple subtraction — see the
      <%= link_to 'Rulebooks', help_page_path('rulebooks'), class: 'no-underline hover:underline hover:underline-offset-2' %>
      reference. Not every page fits that offset cleanly: covers, inserted maps, blank pages, and
      renumbered sections all need manual handling. This page mapping table lets you spot-check
      and correct pages individually. Administrator access only.
    </p>

    <div>
      <p class='text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-highlight mb-4'>Mapping Table</p>
      <dl class='space-y-6'>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>PDF Page</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The page's position in the source PDF.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Default Printed Page</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The printed page number the rulebook's offset would produce for this page, before
            any override.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Override</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Shows a badge if this page has an explicit override or is marked unnumbered;
            otherwise blank, meaning the default printed page applies.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Effective Printed Page</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The page number actually shown to searchers — the override if set,
            <span class='font-mono text-fg-bright'>Unnumbered page</span> if marked as such,
            otherwise the default printed page.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Heading</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The heading detected on the page during extraction, if any.
          </dd>
        </div>

      </dl>
      <p class='mt-4 text-fg-muted'>
        Click a row to open that page and correct it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-highlight mb-4'>Correcting a Page</p>
      <dl class='space-y-6'>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Heading</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Overrides the heading detected during extraction.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Printed Page Override</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            A specific printed page number for this page, independent of the rulebook's offset.
            Use this where the offset gets a page wrong — an inserted map, a renumbered section.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Unnumbered</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Marks the page as having no real printed page number — a cover, a blank page, or
            similar. Unnumbered pages show as
            <span class='font-mono text-fg-bright'>Unnumbered page</span> in search results
            instead of a number.
          </dd>
          <div class='mt-3'>
            <p class='text-fg'>
              A page can have a printed page override <span class='italic'>or</span> be marked
              unnumbered, never both — the form and the database both enforce this.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </dl>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-highlight mb-4'>Extracted Text</p>
      <p class='text-fg'>
        The raw text pulled from the PDF and the normalised text actually indexed for search are
        shown side by side, for diagnosing why a page does or doesn't match a query. If
        extraction picked up unwanted repeated headers, footers, or watermarks, fix that with
        Header/Footer Patterns on the rulebook itself, then rebuild search vectors — no need to
        reimport.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class='pt-2 text-right uppercase font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-fg-muted'>
      REFERENCE 0804RP
    </div>

  </div>
<% end %>
